# Git: commit only when asked; push main only

- Do **not** create commits or push unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. "commit", "push", "push to github").
- Making code changes does **not** imply a commit — leave changes uncommitted until asked.
- When the user does ask to commit/push: use `main` only; do **not** create feature branches for routine work.
- Do not open PRs from side branches unless the user explicitly asks.
- If currently on another branch when asked to push, switch to `main`, bring the needed changes onto `main`, then push `main`.
